    { math: '1 · Two families of generative models', note: 'GANs (2014): a forger and a detective train against each other until forgeries are indistinguishable. Diffusion (2020→): learn to remove noise step by step, then generate by running it backwards. Diffusion won the image race.' },
    { math: '2 · Latent space: the map of meanings', note: 'Generative models compress data into a latent space where nearby points are similar concepts. Interpolating between two latents morphs one face into another — the space itself is a learned geometry of concepts.' },
    { math: '3 · Text-to-image: language steering', note: 'CLIP (2021) learned to match images and text in one space; diffusion conditioned on those embeddings turns sentences into pictures (DALL·E, Stable Diffusion, Midjourney). The prompt is now a programming language for images.' },
    { math: '4 · Copyright and provenance are open problems', note: 'Models trained on artists\' work without consent; outputs resembling training data; watermarks (C2PA provenance) as countermeasures. Courts and markets are still deciding — a live legal frontier, not settled law.' },
